{
  "projectName": "tamagotchi",
  "projectDescription": "Firmware for an ESP32-C3 SuperMini, written in C++ with the Arduino core and built/flashed entirely from the terminal (arduino-cli, ESP32 Arduino core 3.3.8). The firmware (firmware/src) is a modular codebase with display rendering (procedural faces, image/text views, a view manager) on an SSD1306 OLED via U8g2lib, an IMU/MPU6050 motion subsystem (Wire/I2C), a buzzer with jingle assets, command/transport serial protocol layers, mood state, and desktop/free operating modes. Includes standalone bring-up test sketches (led, oled, buzzer, mpu, wifi) plus a Web Serial 3D viewer (firmware/tests/mpu/visualize.html). Also ships '@0xpv/gochi' (v0.1.0), a TypeScript CLI plus local HTTP server for the desk pet, run via tsx on Node (>=18), that talks to the board over serial using the serialport library. The CLI has a daemon/server/client IPC architecture, serial-port discovery, image processing (sharp), an interactive prompt UI (@inquirer/prompts), commander-based command parsing, and per-OS service installers (darwin/linux/windows).",
  "languages": [
